{"lure":{"w":"lure","zh":["誘惑"],"ipa":{"uk":"/lɵː/","us":"/lʊə/"},"ety":[{"n":1,"chain":[{"l":"xno","f":"lure","t":"der"},{"l":"fro","f":"loirre","t":"der"},{"l":"frk","f":"*lōþr","t":"der"},{"l":"gem-pro","f":"*lōþr-","t":"der","g":"invitation, calling"},{"l":"ine-pro","f":"*leh₂-","t":"der","g":"to hide"}],"text":"From Anglo-Norman lure, from Old French loirre (Modern French leurre), from Frankish *lōþr, from Proto-Germanic *lōþr-, perhaps ultimately related to *laþō (“invitation, calling”), or from Proto-Indo-European *leh₂- (“to hide”). Compare English allure, also from Old French. Probably related to German Luder (“bait”).","cog":[{"l":"fr","f":"leurre"},{"l":"en","f":"allure"},{"l":"de","f":"Luder"}]}],"pos":[{"p":"noun","e":0,"senses":[{"d":"Something that tempts or attracts, especially one with a promise of reward or pleasure.","tags":["figurative"],"ex":["How many have with a smile made small account\nOf Beauty and her lures"],"grp":0},{"d":"An artificial bait attached to a fishing line to attract fish.","ex":["the inch-at-a-time flutter of a surface lure"],"grp":1},{"d":"A bunch of feathers attached to a line, used in falconry to recall the hawk.","ex":["My Faulcon now is ſharpe and paſſing emptie, / And til ſhe ſtoope ſhe muſt not be full gorg'd, / For then ſhe never lookes upon her lure."]},{"d":"A velvet smoothing brush."}],"forms":[["pl","lures"]]},{"p":"verb","e":0,"senses":[{"d":"To attract by temptation, appeal, or guile.","tags":["transitive"],"syn":["entice"],"grp":2,"zh":"誘惑"},{"d":"To attract fish with a lure.","tags":["transitive"]},{"d":"To recall a hawk with a lure.","tags":["transitive"]}],"forms":[["3s","lures"],["ing","luring"],["pp","lured"],["past","lured"]]}],"grp":[{"label":"tempting or attractive object","zh":[],"p":"noun","e":0,"tr":{"fr":["fr:attrait"],"it":["it:esca","it:richiamo"],"es":["es:cebo","es:curricán","es:aliciente"],"pt":[]}},{"label":"artificial fishing bait","zh":[],"p":"noun","e":0,"tr":{"fr":["fr:leurre"],"it":["it:e